    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0311" n="277" xml:id="pg277"/>

                <head>124. Telegram From the Embassy in Thailand to the
                        Department of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d124-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1957-01-24T08:00:00+07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 24,
                                1957—8 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2132. SEATO. In informal luncheon conversation
                    yesterday, Acting Foreign Minister Rak speculated might be useful consider
                    consultation in SEATO under Article IV (2) if
                    situation in Laos deteriorated further but such consultation should not be
                    publicized. While desirability formal consultation under Article IV (2) would
                    depend on outcome current developments in Laos, would suggest it highly
                    advisable to inform our SEATO partners within
                    organization framework of U.S. assessment of situation there and of any
                    significant changes U.S. policy. In any event, Laos situation will probably come
                    up during Council’s exchange views at Canberra meeting<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d124-f2"/> and Secretary will doubtless be expected by other members
                    to address himself to it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Bishop</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d124-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d124-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 790.5n–2457. Secret. Repeated to
                    Vientiane.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d124-f2" n="2" xml:id="d124-f2-content">
                <p>The Third Meeting of the SEATO Council had by
                    this time been scheduled for March 11–13 in Canberra.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
